@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/class-diagram
!theme spacelab

title Response Transformers — Strategy for Typed Domain Values

interface ResponseTransformer<R, V> {
  +transform(raw: Response<R>): Response<V>
}
note bottom of ResponseTransformer
  Strategy pattern: converts raw point
  values into typed domain values.
  New transformer providers are supplied to
  the factory without core changes.
end note

class ResponseTransformerFactory {
  +forSensor(type: SensorType): Response<ResponseTransformer>
}

class TemperatureTransformer {}
class TemperatureCelsius {
  +value: double
}
note right of TemperatureCelsius
  Typed value object with range
  validation (Low/HighTemperatureRange)
end note

class Response<T> {
  +status: Status
  +details: String
  +value: T
}

note bottom of Response
  Exception cascade is inherent to Response itself:
  map()/flatMap() short-circuit and propagate an
  EXCEPTION Failure unchanged. Not a separate Strategy
  class — every transformer gets this for free by
  building on Response.map()/flatMap(). Defined in full
  in 01 Communication Client Core.
end note

ResponseTransformerFactory o-- ResponseTransformer : resolves from provider catalog
TemperatureTransformer ..|> ResponseTransformer
TemperatureTransformer ..> TemperatureCelsius : produces
TemperatureTransformer ..> Response : builds on map/flatMap

note as N1
  Used by devices that need typed sensor
  values, e.g. BlaubergMVHR and
  ModbusTemperatureSensor
  (see 06 Example Device Extensions).
end note

@enduml
